{"kind":"request","text":"Reads that wait for a head.\n\nLet a read ask for a minimum head and have the scope hold it briefly until its journal reaches that head, so a client that has just received a receipt can read its own write without polling.\n\nSource: Hugh's request of 28 October 2026, after a review of the alchemy Domain package, whose receipts carry a position that reads and view queries wait for. The planner may attach this to an existing work item or sequence it.\n\nToday: every read returns the head it was read `at`. A client that holds a receipt compares and retries by itself. `followReceipt` reads the entry a receipt names. On the hosted apps the browser polls or reloads.\n\nWanted:\n1. An optional `atLeast` (a sequence number, or a full head) on the summary, items, history and entry reads of ScopeApi, over HTTP and the in-process api. The scope answers at once if its head is at or past it. Otherwise it waits up to a bound and answers when the head arrives, or answers `unavailable` with reason `behind` and its current head when the bound passes. A head from another incarnation is `wrong-incarnation`.\n2. The bound is a member of Bounds. A waiting read holds no storage transaction and does not block the turn.\n3. The client handle's reads accept a receipt and pass its position; `followReceipt` uses it instead of retrying.\n4. Reads write nothing, so replay is unaffected; the Readers port decides who may read, as today.\n5. A witness on a real scope: a read with a future head waits and returns the entry when it is written; a read past the bound answers `behind`.","body":{"conditions":"Landed on main with the read option in ScopeApi, HTTP and the in-process api, the client support and the real-scope witness; or superseded by a planner act naming the request that carries this work.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}